## Lore

Reaver Assassins are the Warlords'' commandos and executioners. They are
picked out and trained at remote sites through brutal obstacle courses, hand
to hand fighting and surprise attacks sprung on them in their sleep, all of
it meant to prove a killer instinct and to teach that a calm head wins. What
comes out the other end reacts faster than almost anyone in a War Camp.

They are not spies. Stealth and deception are only the means of getting
close enough to kill, and their real trades are weapons, demolitions,
torture and intimidation. They draw the search and destroy missions, the
sabotage, the prison breaks and the surgical strikes, alone, in pairs, or as
the one or two killers attached to a covert team. Many live for years inside
mercenary companies, bandit gangs and the Black Market as double agents,
quietly removing whoever threatens their Warlord and getting rich on the side.

Most enjoy the work and the reputation, and even Smoke Soldiers are uneasy
around them. They are also the least loyal troops a Warlord has: plenty
skim their tribute, and a good number eventually turn freelance. A small
minority have seen so much death that they have grown merciful, and kill
quickly and cleanly when they must kill at all.

## GM Notes

Printed as "O.C.C. & NPC Villain"; it is a playable class. Alignment is
technically any, but roughly nine in ten are anarchist or evil.

Hand to Hand: Assassin cannot be exchanged. Automatic Dodge costs no melee
action but still needs a successful D20 roll with the usual bonuses.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: one weapon for each W.P., each gun
with four extra clips and a telescopic scope with a passive nightvision
sight; 1D4+2 grenades of choice; a pad of paper, a grappling hook, a set of
clothing, a long winter coat or cloak, commando face paint and odds and
ends. The vehicle is a hovercycle or another basic vehicle.

Money is 1D4x1,000 credits plus 1D4x1,000 credits of stolen booty. Salary is
about 800-1,000 credits a month, and the assassin usually keeps 33% of any
booty picked up on the job so long as taking it does not endanger the mission.

Bionics, typical for a mostly human, lightly augmented assassin: one bionic
hand and/or arm (P.S. 16-20) with a Fingerjack, a Laser Finger Blaster (1D4
M.D., 300 ft/91 m), one hand weapon or feature of choice and two arm weapons
or features of choice; a concealed Bionic Jaw and Reinforced Skull with a
built-in radio receiver and transmitter and a built-in language translator;
Clock Calendar; Cyber-Disguise Type AA-1; Gyro-Compass; and two lung
implants, an Oxygen Storage Cell and a Toxic Filter. The amount varies: 22%
are partial cyborgs, 12% are Light Machines usually disguised as human, and
4% are heavy full conversion cyborgs.

On assignment the assassin may be issued any type of weapon (Triax and other
imports included), explosives with limited access to Fusion Blocks, special
equipment, vehicles, disguises, false papers, and money, gold or gems for
bribes. Secret resources: none to start, but contacts like a Smoke Soldier''s
can be built through play, and one of the first will be an arms dealer or
smuggler.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'reaver-assassin');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
